Group type: small
Definition: informal voluntary association of three or more people. Members chose each other. No institutional structure, no assigned or inherited membership. Every member has a personal bond with every other.
Test: remove any one member and the rest still form a group.
Include: friend circles, companies formed by choice, conspiracies, travelling parties, circles gathered around a mentor or a shared pursuit.
Exclude: any group a character was placed into, admitted to, or born into.
Exclude pairs. A bond between two people is a relationship, not a group, and must never be returned here. Every returned group has at least three members.
Coverage: return every such group you can identify, including minor, short-lived and arc-specific ones. Include adult, background and antagonist characters, not only the main cast.
Do not force characters into groups. Many characters belong to no informal group at all and are simply omitted.